BT /F1 10 Tf 12 TL 56 760 Td (Rosterforge) Tj T* () Tj T* (Rosterforge Executive Summary) Tj T* () Tj T* (Problem) Tj T* () Tj T* (Small and mid-sized caterers run on thin margins and tight timelines, and their largest) Tj T* (operational risk is a short-staffed event. In interviews with 31 caterers and event-staffing) Tj T* (managers in our university's metro area, 26 said they had experienced a same-week staffing gap) Tj T* (in the previous quarter, and 19 said they had lost revenue or paid rush premiums because of) Tj T* (one. A typical event needs between four and fifteen part-time workers, such as bartenders,) Tj T* (servers, and setup or breakdown crews. Cancellations of 10 to 15 percent are normal, and most) Tj T* (caterers fill the gaps through group text threads, calls to former employees, and referrals.) Tj T* (This is slow, depends on a few individuals, and leaves no record of who is reliable. Payment is) Tj T* (a second friction: workers are paid by cash or by payroll that arrives one to two weeks after) Tj T* (the shift, which makes the best workers less willing to take short-notice work.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Solution) Tj T* () Tj T* (Rosterforge is a mobile and web app that turns an unfilled shift into a filled one within) Tj T* (hours. A caterer posts a shift with role, start time, duration, location and hourly rate. The) Tj T* (app notifies matching workers who have set their availability and role preferences, ranks them) Tj T* (by proximity, past ratings and reliability, and confirms the first acceptance. On the day,) Tj T* (workers check in with a location-verified tap. When the caterer confirms hours at the end of) Tj T* (the shift, the worker is paid immediately through a payments partner, and the caterer is billed) Tj T* (the same amount plus our fee. Caterers can also build a private roster of favorite workers who) Tj T* (are offered shifts first, which gives them the convenience of their existing contacts with the) Tj T* (reach of a larger pool.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Market) Tj T* () Tj T* (We are starting with caterers serving weddings, corporate events and private parties in a) Tj T* (single metropolitan area. Using public industry counts and our interviews, we estimate roughly) Tj T* (420 catering businesses in our launch metro, of which about 250 employ part-time event staff.) Tj T* (If the average such caterer books 60 events per year and fills eight roles per event, the metro) Tj T* (represents about 120,000 shifts per year. At an average shift value of 140 dollars, that is) Tj T* (roughly 16.8 million dollars in annual labor spend in our beachhead market. Our national) Tj T* (estimate, scaling by population from the same assumptions, is a staffing spend in the low) Tj T* (billions of dollars. These figures are rough, built from a small interview sample, and we plan) Tj T* (to refine them during the pilot.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Business Model) Tj T* () Tj T* (We charge caterers a service fee of 12 percent of the shift's labor cost, collected on top of) Tj T* (worker pay, and workers pay nothing. Early pricing is based on conversations rather than tests,) Tj T* (and we expect to adjust it after the pilot. At an average shift value of 140 dollars, revenue) Tj T* (is about 16.80 dollars per shift before payment-processing costs of roughly 2.5 percent,) Tj T* (leaving a contribution margin near 13 dollars per shift. A caterer filling 40 shifts per month) Tj T* (through Rosterforge would generate about 520 dollars in monthly contribution. We assume an) Tj T* (acquisition cost of 400 dollars per caterer through direct outreach and referrals, which) Tj T* (implies a payback of under one month if usage reaches that level. We have not yet validated) Tj T* (that usage level beyond our first client. We may later add a premium tier with roster analytics) Tj T* (and compliance tools.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Competition) Tj T* () Tj T* (The space is crowded. General-purpose shift-scheduling tools serve restaurants and retail but) Tj T* (do not supply workers. On-demand staffing marketplaces supply workers across many industries) Tj T* (but tend to focus on warehousing and hospitality agencies with minimum contracts and higher) Tj T* (fees. Traditional staffing agencies charge markups of 30 to 50 percent and respond in days.) Tj ET
