e project 12 active) Tj T* (caterers, 1,800 shifts per month by month twelve, and monthly revenue of about 30,000 dollars) Tj T* (by year end. These projections assume rates of signup and repeat use that we have only observed) Tj T* (with one client, and we regard them as targets rather than forecasts. Our largest costs are) Tj T* (founder-led sales, payments and background-check fees, and part-time development help.) Tj T* () Tj T* (What We Ask For) Tj T* () Tj T* (We are applying for the competition's prize funding and mentoring. A 25,000 dollar award would) Tj T* (let us run a structured three-month pilot with 8 to 10 additional caterers, pay for background) Tj T* (checks and payment-processing minimums, and engage legal counsel to review worker) Tj T* (classification rules, which we know vary by state and represent a real risk to our model.) Tj T* (Beyond funding, we would value introductions to caterers and venue managers, advice on labor) Tj T* (compliance, and feedback on our pricing. Our goal is to show, by the end of the pilot, repeat) Tj T* (usage by at least six caterers and a fill rate above 90 percent, which would put us in a) Tj T* (position to raise a seed round.) Tj ET
